    reg {
        name = "Channel scaler coefficient table address 3.1 (VPSS_HAL_SetChnSclCoeff)";
        desc = "Node image offset 0x3E4. Four table addresses per channel slot (SetChnSclCoeff takes four pointers and requires each 16-byte aligned; order +0 hor luma, +4 ver luma, +8 hor chroma, +12 ver chroma: PROVEN, GenSclCfg). Slot order as CH_IMG_SIZE. COEFFICIENT TABLE FORMAT (vendor pass 2026-11-11, InitSclCoeff and vpss_scl*coef_to_dut, HIGH for the packing, MEDIUM for which pointer is which): the four tables of a channel are horizontal luma (8 taps), horizontal chroma (4 taps), vertical luma (6 taps) and vertical chroma (4 taps) (pointer order PROVEN from GenSclCfg 0x14924, which fills the four pointers: +0 horizontal luma, +4 vertical luma, +8 horizontal chroma, +12 vertical chroma). Each table has 17 phases (1/16 pel steps, phase 0..16); a tap is a signed 10-bit value (two's complement masked to 10 bits), unity = 512 (every phase sums to 512 in the vendor tables, phase 0 of a few tables sums to 511). Packing (little endian 32-bit words): 8-tap luma = 3 words per phase: w0 = c0 | c1<<10 | c2<<20, w1 = c3 | c4<<10 | c5<<20, w2 = c6 | c7<<10 (51 words, 204 bytes); 6-tap = 3 words per phase, taps paired as c0 | c1<<16 (51 words); 4-tap = 2 words per phase, c0 | c1<<16, c2 | c3<<16 (34 words, 136 bytes); a 2-tap converter exists (1 word per phase, 17 words) but is unused by InitSclCoeff. The vendor allocates one 5888-byte (0x1700) buffer and places tables at 256-byte slots: slots 0-5 horizontal luma (lanczos3, cubic, lanczos2, 3M_a19, 2M_a05, 1.5M_a05 low-pass variants), 6-10 horizontal chroma 4-tap, 11-17 vertical luma 6-tap, 18-22 vertical chroma 4-tap. Slot selection (PROVEN, GenSclCfg 0x14924; r = output/input size, horizontal 12.20, vertical 20.12): horizontal luma: r > 1 slot 0, r == 1 slot 1, 0.5 <= r < 1 slot 2, 1/3 < r < 0.5 slot 3, 0.25 <= r <= 1/3 slot 4, r < 0.25 slot 5; horizontal chroma: r > 1 slot 6, == 1 slot 7, 0.5 <= r < 1 slot 6, 1/3 < r < 0.5 slot 9, else slot 10; vertical luma: r > 1 slot 11, == 1 slot 12, >= 0.75 slot 13, >= 0.5 slot 14, > 1/3 slot 15, >= 0.25 slot 16, else slot 17; vertical chroma: r > 1 slot 18, == 1 slot 19, >= 0.5 slot 18, > 1/3 slot 21, else slot 22. The pre-scaler pointers (+0x3A0 horizontal, +0x3A8 vertical) are always slot 2 and slot 6. Steps (in/out): horizontal luma = (in << 20) / out, vertical luma = (in << 12) / out, chroma the same with the chroma sizes; the 28-bit step fields of the 8-word scaler blocks (0x204/0x208 + 0x20*ch) take these (INFERRED which of the two words is which). Not verified on hardware.  Source: hi3520D_vpss.ko. Not verified on hardware.";
